tests/ci_shard.d/ -- drop-in additions to the CI test shard (#328)

To put a test file into the per-PR fast shard, do NOT edit tests/ci_shard.txt
(every PR appending to the same spot of that file conflicted with every other).
Add ONE new file here instead, named after your issue:

    tests/ci_shard.d/<issue>-<slug>.txt        e.g.  328-shard-list.txt

containing one test path per line:

    # why these files are fresh-clone safe (optional comment)
    tests/test_my_feature.py

Rules -- enforced by tools/dev/shard_list.py, which tools/dev/session_ci.sh
(the session-hosted CI) and the reference .github/workflows/ci.yml both use:
  * one path per line; blank lines and whole-line `#` comments are ignored;
  * entries must be plain test files: tests/[A-Za-z0-9_./-]+.py, no `..`,
    no pytest flags -- one bad entry refuses the whole shard (CI fails loudly);
  * file names: [A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*.txt (portable; this README is ignored);
  * the shard = tests/ci_shard.txt in its own order (tests/test_schema_gate.py
    stays first), then every *.txt here sorted by file name; a path listed
    twice anywhere runs once (first occurrence wins);
  * only list files that are green in a FRESH CLONE (no samples/, extracted/,
    vendor/, viewer login, ifcopenshell) -- see the header of tests/ci_shard.txt.

See the merged list:   python3 tools/dev/shard_list.py --print
Run it like CI does:   .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q -- $(python3 tools/dev/shard_list.py --print)
tests/test_shard_list.py pins these rules and that every listed path exists.
